@page "/"

<PageTitle>The Singularity Workshop | Software Engineering & Systems Architecture</PageTitle>

<div class="workshop-home">
    <section class="hero-section">
        <div class="hero-grid"></div>
        <div class="hero-content">
            <div class="status-line">
                <span class="status-dot"></span>
                THE SINGULARITY WORKSHOP IS OPEN FOR BUSINESS
            </div>

            <p class="eyebrow">SOFTWARE ENGINEERING · SYSTEMS ARCHITECTURE · AUTOMATION · R&amp;D</p>

            <h1>You've got a hard problem.<br /><span>Show me.</span></h1>

            <p class="hero-lead">
                The Workshop builds the machinery behind complicated software systems —
                from high-performance .NET architecture and automation to AI agents,
                simulation, interactive applications, and the strange problems that don't fit neatly into a job title.
            </p>

            <div class="hero-actions">
                <a class="workshop-button primary" href="engagement">Start an Engagement <span>→</span></a>
                <a class="workshop-button secondary" href="#proof">See What We've Built <span>↓</span></a>
            </div>

            <div class="hero-note">
                <strong>One hour can be enough to find out.</strong>
                Show us the workflow, the bottleneck, the ugly code, or the impossible requirement.
                We'll determine what can be automated, redesigned, measured, or built.
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-orbit" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="orbit orbit-one"></div>
            <div class="orbit orbit-two"></div>
            <div class="orbit-core">
                <span>TSW</span>
                <small>BUILD · MEASURE · PROVE</small>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="proof-strip" id="proof">
        <div class="proof-item">
            <strong>15+</strong>
            <span>years inside complex AEC/BIM workflows</span>
        </div>
        <div class="proof-item">
            <strong>66K</strong>
            <span>autonomous agents stress-tested in a real-time FSM simulation</span>
        </div>
        <div class="proof-item">
            <strong>1</strong>
            <span>principle: measure the thing before making promises about it</span>
        </div>
        <div class="proof-item">
            <strong>∞</strong>
            <span>interesting problems that don't fit inside a résumé checkbox</span>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section dark-section">
        <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="eyebrow">THE WORKSHOP</p>
            <h2>We don't sell a job title.<br /><span>We solve the problem.</span></h2>
            <p>
                The useful question isn't whether a problem is technically "BIM," "C#," "AI," or "Unity."
                The useful question is whether the machinery can be made better.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="capability-grid">
            <article class="capability-card">
                <div class="card-number">01</div>
                <h3>Automation &amp; Integration</h3>
                <p>
                    Replace repetitive human workflows with reliable software. APIs, Revit/Dynamo,
                    data pipelines, document generation, desktop tooling, integrations, and the awkward glue between systems.
                </p>
                <span class="card-tag">MAKE THE WORKFLOW DISAPPEAR</span>
            </article>

            <article class="capability-card featured">
                <div class="card-number">02</div>
                <h3>Software Architecture</h3>
                <p>
                    Untangle systems that have grown beyond their original design. State, lifecycle,
                    dependencies, performance, memory, concurrency, modularity, and the architecture required to make complexity manageable.
                </p>
                <span class="card-tag">DESIGN FOR THE NEXT MILLION STATES</span>
            </article>

            <article class="capability-card">
                <div class="card-number">03</div>
                <h3>AI &amp; Agent Systems</h3>
                <p>
                    Build the deterministic machinery around probabilistic intelligence: tool discovery,
                    command boundaries, grammar, validation, execution, feedback loops, and systems that can actually do things.
                </p>
                <span class="card-tag">INTELLIGENCE NEEDS MACHINERY</span>
            </article>

            <article class="capability-card">
                <div class="card-number">04</div>
                <h3>Performance Engineering</h3>
                <p>
                    Stop guessing. Benchmark the hot path, measure allocations, expose scaling behavior,
                    identify bottlenecks, and turn performance claims into numbers that can survive scrutiny.
                </p>
                <span class="card-tag">MEASURE · OPTIMIZE · PROVE</span>
            </article>

            <article class="capability-card">
                <div class="card-number">05</div>
                <h3>Interactive &amp; Simulation Systems</h3>
                <p>
                    Unity, WebAssembly, visualization, game systems, simulations, and experiences built on
                    the same architectural discipline used for serious software.
                </p>
                <span class="card-tag">FROM MODEL TO EXPERIENCE</span>
            </article>

            <article class="capability-card">
                <div class="card-number">06</div>
                <h3>The Weird Stuff</h3>
                <p>
                    Legacy systems. Impossible integrations. A bug nobody can reproduce. A workflow nobody has
                    bothered to automate. If it is difficult because it crosses boundaries, that's exactly where we want to look.
                </p>
                <span class="card-tag">BRING THE WEIRD PROBLEM</span>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section evidence-section">
        <div class="section-heading centered">
            <p class="eyebrow">DON'T TAKE OUR WORD FOR IT</p>
            <h2>There is a workshop<br /><span>behind the workshop.</span></h2>
            <p>
                The Workshop isn't a consulting brand wrapped around a résumé. These are real systems,
                real experiments, real benchmarks, and real software being built in public.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="evidence-grid">
            <a class="evidence-card" href="https://github.com/TrentBest/FSM_API" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                <span class="evidence-label">OPEN SOURCE</span>
                <h3>FSM_API</h3>
                <p>A software-agnostic finite state machine API for .NET, designed around decoupled behavior, scalable execution, and deterministic logic.</p>
                <span class="evidence-link">Explore the repository →</span>
            </a>

            <a class="evidence-card" href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/TheSingularityWorkshop.FSM_API" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                <span class="evidence-label">SHIPPED SOFTWARE</span>
                <h3>Production Package</h3>
                <p>The FSM_API is distributed as a real .NET package — because architecture is more useful when someone else can actually install it.</p>
                <span class="evidence-link">View the package →</span>
            </a>

            <a class="evidence-card" href="https://coderlegion.com/26350/benchmarking-the-fsm-pure-strings-already-fast-and-about-to-get-faster" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                <span class="evidence-label">MEASURED</span>
                <h3>The Benchmark</h3>
                <p>Performance work published with measurements instead of mythology: scaling behavior, allocations, and the cost of architectural choices.</p>
                <span class="evidence-link">Read the benchmark →</span>
            </a>

            <a class="evidence-card" href="https://coderlegion.com/26524/from-rug-pull-to-runtime-why-im-open-for-business-and-building-the-future-of-ugc" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                <span class="evidence-label">OPEN FOR BUSINESS</span>
                <h3>From Rug Pull to Runtime</h3>
                <p>The Workshop is no longer waiting for the next contract to define what gets built. We are building the future and inviting clients into the forge.</p>
                <span class="evidence-link">Read the story →</span>
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section aec-section">
        <div class="aec-panel">
            <div class="aec-copy">
                <p class="eyebrow">THE UNFAIR ADVANTAGE</p>
                <h2>Deep domain experience.<br /><span>Software-engineering mindset.</span></h2>
                <p>
                    More than a decade inside AEC/BIM environments means we understand what it feels like when
                    software gets in the way of the work. That experience is useful far beyond BIM.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Revit, Dynamo, CAD ecosystems, project data, standards, automation, and enterprise workflows
                    taught us how to find the real problem hiding underneath the requested feature.
                </p>
                <a class="text-link" href="about-us">Meet the Workshop →</a>
            </div>
            <div class="aec-quote">
                <div class="quote-mark">“</div>
                <p>Show me the workflow that is costing your team time.</p>
                <small>We'll figure out whether it should be automated, redesigned, or left alone.</small>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="engagement-section">
        <div class="engagement-inner">
            <p class="eyebrow">NOW ACCEPTING ENGAGEMENTS</p>
            <h2>Bring us the problem.</h2>
            <p>
                Start with a conversation. We can spend an hour understanding the workflow, identifying the real
                bottleneck, and determining whether there is a credible path to a useful solution.
            </p>
            <div class="engagement-actions">
                <a class="workshop-button primary large" href="engagement">Schedule an Engagement <span>→</span></a>
                <a class="workshop-button ghost large" href="mailto:thesingularityworkshop@gmail.com?subject=The%20Singularity%20Workshop%20-%20Engagement%20Inquiry">Email the Workshop <span>✉</span></a>
            </div>
            <p class="engagement-fine-print">No sales maze. No need to know the solution before you call. Tell us what hurts.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="workshop-footer">
        <div>
            <strong>THE SINGULARITY WORKSHOP</strong>
            <span>Forging Software for the Singularity.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="footer-links">
            <a href="engagement">Work With Us</a>
            <a href="demos">Explore the Demos</a>
            <a href="about-us">About</a>
            <a href="support">Support</a>
        </div>
    </footer>
</div>

<style>
    .workshop-home {
        --ink: #08070d;
        --panel: #11101a;
        --panel-2: #171522;
        --cyan: #00ffcc;
        --cyan-soft: rgba(0, 255, 204, 0.18);
        --magenta: #ff2bd6;
        --violet: #9b5cff;
        --muted: #a8a6b7;
        background: var(--ink);
        color: #fff;
        min-height: 100vh;
        margin: -1.5rem -1.5rem 0;
        font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    }

    .hero-section {
        min-height: 760px;
        position: relative;
        overflow: hidden;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        padding: 6rem 8vw;
        background: radial-gradient(circle at 75% 45%, rgba(155, 92, 255, 0.18), transparent 28%),
                    radial-gradient(circle at 20% 15%, rgba(0, 255, 204, 0.10), transparent 32%),
                    linear-gradient(135deg, #07060b 0%, #0d0915 48%, #07060b 100%);
        border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,255,204,.18);
    }

    .hero-grid {
        position: absolute;
        inset: 0;
        opacity: .18;
        background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(0,255,204,.15) 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(0,255,204,.15) 1px, transparent 1px);
        background-size: 52px 52px;
        mask-image: linear-gradient(to right, black, transparent 75%);
    }

    .hero-content { position: relative; z-index: 2; max-width: 800px; }

    .status-line, .eyebrow { letter-spacing: .18em; font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 800; }
    .status-line { color: var(--cyan); margin-bottom: 1.5rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: .65rem; }
    .status-dot { width: 9px; height: 9px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--cyan); box-shadow: 0 0 18px var(--cyan); animation: pulse 1.7s infinite; }
    .eyebrow { color: #8f8ca2; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }

    .hero-section h1 { font-size: clamp(3.4rem, 7vw, 6.8rem); line-height: .92; letter-spacing: -.055em; margin: 0 0 2rem; font-weight: 900; }
    .hero-section h1 span, .section-heading h2 span, .aec-copy h2 span { color: var(--cyan); text-shadow: 0 0 30px rgba(0,255,204,.25); }
    .hero-lead { color: #d0ceda; font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.8vw, 1.35rem); line-height: 1.75; max-width: 760px; }

    .hero-actions, .engagement-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 2.25rem; }
    .workshop-button { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1.5rem; padding: 1rem 1.4rem; border-radius: 5px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .04em; transition: transform .2s, box-shadow .2s, background .2s; }
    .workshop-button.primary { color: #04110d; background: var(--cyan); box-shadow: 0 0 30px rgba(0,255,204,.22); }
    .workshop-button.primary:hover { color: #04110d; transform: translateY(-3px); box-shadow: 0 10px 35px rgba(0,255,204,.35); }
    .workshop-button.secondary, .workshop-button.ghost { color: #fff; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.22); background: rgba(255,255,255,.03); }
    .workshop-button.secondary:hover, .workshop-button.ghost:hover { color: #fff; transform: translateY(-3px); border-color: var(--cyan); }
    .workshop-button.large { padding: 1.15rem 1.6rem; }

    .hero-note { margin-top: 2.5rem; max-width: 680px; color: #8f8ca2; line-height: 1.7; font-size: .92rem; border-left: 2px solid var(--magenta); padding-left: 1rem; }
    .hero-note strong { color: #fff; }

    .hero-orbit { position: absolute; right: 4vw; width: 480px; height: 480px; display: grid; place-items: center; opacity: .9; }
    .orbit { position: absolute; border: 1px solid rgba(0,255,204,.28); border-radius: 50%; }
    .orbit-one { width: 100%; height: 42%; transform: rotate(-24deg); box-shadow: 0 0 40px rgba(0,255,204,.08); }
    .orbit-two { width: 74%; height: 74%; transform: rotate(35deg); border-color: rgba(255,43,214,.28); }
    .orbit-core { width: 150px; height: 150px; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; align-items: center; background: radial-gradient(circle, #211b35, #09080e 70%); border: 1px solid var(--cyan); box-shadow: 0 0 55px rgba(0,255,204,.18), inset 0 0 35px rgba(155,92,255,.18); }
    .orbit-core span { font-size: 2.4rem; font-weight: 900; color: #fff; }
    .orbit-core small { color: var(--cyan); font-size: .52rem; letter-spacing: .12em; }

    .proof-strip { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); background: #0d0c13; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08); }
    .proof-item { padding: 2rem 1.5rem; text-align: center; border-right: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08); }
    .proof-item:last-child { border-right: 0; }
    .proof-item strong { display: block; font-size: 2rem; color: var(--cyan); }
    .proof-item span { display: block; margin: .45rem auto 0; max-width: 220px; color: #8f8ca2; font-size: .78rem; line-height: 1.5; }

    .section { padding: 7rem 8vw; }
    .dark-section { background: #08070d; }
    .section-heading { max-width: 780px; margin-bottom: 3.5rem; }
    .section-heading.centered { text-align: center; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
    .section-heading h2, .aec-copy h2 { font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 4.5rem); line-height: .98; letter-spacing: -.04em; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; font-weight: 900; }
    .section-heading > p:last-child, .aec-copy > p { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.8; font-size: 1.05rem; }

    .capability-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1rem; }
    .capability-card { position: relative; min-height: 300px; padding: 2rem; background: linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(255,255,255,.045), rgba(255,255,255,.015)); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09); border-radius: 8px; transition: transform .2s, border-color .2s; }
    .capability-card:hover { transform: translateY(-5px); border-color: rgba(0,255,204,.45); }
    .capability-card.featured { border-color: rgba(0,255,204,.38); background: radial-gradient(circle at 100% 0%, rgba(0,255,204,.10), transparent 42%), #11101a; }
    .card-number { color: var(--magenta); font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: .75rem; letter-spacing: .15em; }
    .capability-card h3 { font-size: 1.35rem; margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem; }
    .capability-card p { color: #aaa7b6; line-height: 1.7; font-size: .94rem; }
    .card-tag { position: absolute; left: 2rem; bottom: 1.7rem; color: var(--cyan); font-size: .62rem; letter-spacing: .13em; font-weight: 800; }

    .evidence-section { background: linear-gradient(180deg, #10101a, #08070d); }
    .evidence-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 1rem; max-width: 1100px; margin: auto; }
    .evidence-card { display: block; color: #fff; text-decoration: none; padding: 2rem; min-height: 245px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1); background: rgba(255,255,255,.025); border-radius: 8px; transition: transform .2s, border-color .2s, background .2s; }
    .evidence-card:hover { color: #fff; transform: translateY(-4px); border-color: var(--violet); background: rgba(155,92,255,.07); }
    .evidence-label { color: var(--magenta); font-size: .65rem; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: .16em; }
    .evidence-card h3 { font-size: 1.8rem; margin: 1rem 0 .8rem; }
    .evidence-card p { color: #aaa7b6; line-height: 1.7; }
    .evidence-link { color: var(--cyan); font-size: .82rem; font-weight: 800; }

    .aec-section { background: #08070d; }
    .aec-panel { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.3fr .7fr; gap: 4rem; max-width: 1200px; margin: auto; align-items: center; }
    .aec-quote { padding: 3rem; border: 1px solid rgba(0,255,204,.22); background: radial-gradient(circle at 0 0, rgba(0,255,204,.08), transparent 60%), #0e0d15; border-radius: 8px; }
    .quote-mark { font-size: 5rem; line-height: .5; color: var(--magenta); }
    .aec-quote p { font-size: 1.65rem; line-height: 1.3; font-weight: 800; margin: 2rem 0 1rem; }
    .aec-quote small { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; }
    .text-link { display: inline-block; margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--cyan); font-weight: 800; text-decoration: none; }

    .engagement-section { padding: 7rem 8vw; text-align: center; background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 0%, rgba(255,43,214,.14), transparent 38%), linear-gradient(135deg, #0e0a16, #07060b); border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,43,214,.18); }
    .engagement-inner { max-width: 900px; margin: auto; }
    .engagement-section h2 { font-size: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem); line-height: .9; margin: .5rem 0 1.5rem; letter-spacing: -.05em; }
    .engagement-section > .engagement-inner > p:not(.eyebrow):not(.engagement-fine-print) { color: #b7b3c1; font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.8; max-width: 720px; margin: auto; }
    .engagement-actions { justify-content: center; }
    .engagement-fine-print { color: #6e6a7b; font-size: .78rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }

    .workshop-footer { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 2rem; padding: 2.5rem 8vw; background: #050509; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08); }
    .workshop-footer strong, .workshop-footer span { display: block; }
    .workshop-footer strong { font-size: .78rem; letter-spacing: .14em; }
    .workshop-footer span { color: #6e6a7b; margin-top: .4rem; font-size: .8rem; }
    .footer-links { display: flex; gap: 1.25rem; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: flex-end; }
    .footer-links a { color: #8f8ca2; text-decoration: none; font-size: .8rem; }
    .footer-links a:hover { color: var(--cyan); }

    @@keyframes pulse { 0%, 100% { transform: scale(1); opacity: 1; } 50% { transform: scale(.7); opacity: .55; } }

    @@media (max-width: 1100px) {
        .hero-orbit { opacity: .28; right: -130px; }
        .capability-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
    }

    @@media (max-width: 760px) {
        .hero-section { min-height: auto; padding: 5rem 7vw 4rem; }
        .hero-orbit { display: none; }
        .proof-strip { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }
        .proof-item:nth-child(2) { border-right: 0; }
        .capability-grid, .evidence-grid, .aec-panel { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
        .section { padding: 5rem 7vw; }
        .workshop-footer { flex-direction: column; }
        .footer-links { justify-content: flex-start; }
    }

    @@media (max-width: 480px) {
        .proof-strip { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
        .proof-item { border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08); }
        .capability-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
        .hero-actions, .engagement-actions { flex-direction: column; }
        .workshop-button { width: 100%; }
    }
</style>
